-- title:
--   Separable annihilator for good Hecke and diamond operators on J₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58), i.e. that for every prime $\ell$ the Hecke input package `HeckeInputsOneAlong` holds over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at level $M$ and $\ell$ (a defined $\beta$-datum, integrality of the $\alpha$- and $\beta$-correspondences, principal divisors for the base-changed $X_1/X_0$ function field, finiteness along $\alpha$, together with the fundamental identity and the norm formula), and that for every $d$ coprime to $M$ there is a diamond automorphism of the function field `x1FunctionField M` in the sense of `IsDiamondAut` and an automorphism of `x1FunctionFieldBar M` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ base-changed from `diamondAut M d`; assume also [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54), that the endomorphisms `heckeDiamondGenBar M i` of the degree-zero divisor class group `JOne M` of the base-changed function field commute pairwise. Equip `JOne M` with the resulting module structure `heckeModuleOneBar M` over `HeckeAlgOne = MvPolynomial (Nat.Primes ⊕ ℕ) ℤ`. Then for every $w$ in the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of `HeckeAlgOne` generated by the variables `heckeGenOne ℓ` and `diamondGen ℓ` with $\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$, there is a non-zero $P \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose image in $\mathbb{Q}[X]$ is separable such that the element $P(w)$ of `HeckeAlgOne` annihilates every $x \in$ `JOne M`.
--
--   This is the semisimplicity statement for the subring generated by the good Hecke operators $T_\ell$ and diamond operators $\langle\ell\rangle$ ($\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$) acting on the Jacobian of $X_1(M)$: each such operator is killed by a squarefree integral polynomial. It is used in the analysis of the kernel of the Hecke ideal attached to a primitive form on the Tate module of $J_1(M)$, one of the inputs to level lowering.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_separable_aeval_smul_eq_zero_jOne_of_mem_adjoin_good.lean

